{## The standalone laptop guide for one OS (only_os). The body is en/laptop.md.j2. ##}
{% set NP = "Not provided" %}
{% set osname = {"windows": "Windows", "macos": "macOS", "linux": "Linux"} %}
{% set system = a.get("environment") or f.domain %}
{% set doc = a.get("document") or {} %}
{% set bast = a.get("bast") or {} %}
{% set client = a.get("client") or {} %}
{% set vendor = a.get("vendor") or {} %}
{% set dns = a.get("dns") or {} %}
{% set client_ca = (a.get("tls") or {}).get("client_ca") %}
{% set docnumber = doc.get("number") or NP %}
{% set docversion = doc.get("version") or "1.0" %}
{% set docclass = doc.get("classification") or "CONFIDENTIAL" %}
{% set docdate = (bast.date | date) if bast.get("date") else NP %}
{% set mine = people | selectattr("os", "equalto", only_os) | list %}
---
title: {{ "Laptop Access Guide" | q }}
subtitle: {{ (osname[only_os] ~ " · " ~ system) | q }}
short-title: {{ ("Laptop Access Guide (" ~ osname[only_os] ~ ")") | q }}
lang: en
docnumber: {{ docnumber | q }}
version: {{ docversion | q }}
date: {{ (docdate if bast.get("date") else (today | date)) | q }}
classification: {{ docclass | q }}
numbered: true
{% if draft %}
draft: true
{% endif %}
labels: {page: "Page", of: "of", toc: "Contents"}
cover:
  kicker: {{ "LAPTOP ACCESS GUIDE" | q }}
{% if logo.vendor %}
  logo: {{ logo.vendor | q }}
{% endif %}
  rows:
    - {label: "Client", value: {{ (client.get("name") or NP) | q }}}
    - {label: "Vendor", value: {{ (vendor.get("name") or NP) | q }}}
    - {label: "System", value: {{ (system ~ " (" ~ f.domain ~ ")" if a.get("environment") else f.domain) | q }}}
    - {label: "Laptop", value: {{ osname[only_os] | q }}}
    - {label: "Document number", value: {{ docnumber | q }}}
    - {label: "Version", value: {{ docversion | q }}}
    - {label: "Date", value: {{ docdate | q }}}
    - {label: "Classification", value: {{ docclass | q }}}
  footer: {{ ("Made with dejavu " ~ dejavu ~ " from ansibro " ~ (f.ansibro.version or "?") ~ ". This guide contains no passwords; they are only in the encrypted credentials file.") | q }}
---

# Access from your laptop ({{ osname[only_os] }}) {#guide}

This guide shows how to reach {{ system | md }} ({{ f.domain }}) of {{ client.name | md if client.get("name") else NP }} from a {{ osname[only_os] }} laptop: the web pages, the passwords and, for operators, the servers. It is part of the handover by {{ vendor.name | md if vendor.get("name") else NP }}. The technical documentation has the full details.

{% if mine %}
It is meant for: {% for p in mine %}{{ p.name | md if p.name else NP }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}


{% endif %}
You need these files from the handover pack: the credentials file, ssh_config.txt{{ ", hosts.txt" if dns.get("mode") == "hosts" }}{{ (", " ~ slug ~ "-ca.crt") if f.ca_file or client_ca }}, and the passphrase, which is given to you separately.

{% include "en/laptop.md.j2" %}
